A||N||9||fierovette||Balance rear wheels?||||5||
Z||000000||fierovette||08-16-2001||01:34 PM||||Is it necessary to balance the rear wheels? Got the ugly weights on the rears, can I just pop them off or should I bring them to the tire man and see if he can balance them with the weights on the inside?||||reg||5
Z||000001||V8Dreamer||08-16-2001||03:21 PM||||Unless you wish to drive a giant vibrator, I'd recommend having the tires re-balanced with the weights on the inside......I had unbalanced tires in the rear and that 6 hour trip to see my gf at school sucked at highway speeds, plus it'll assist anything that could possibly rattle in doing so.<P>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steve Normington||08-16-2001||03:22 PM||||The rear wheels need to be balanced. Ideally, half of the weights should be on the outside and half should be on the inside, but having them all on the inside shouldn't be too bad.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieronv||08-16-2001||03:24 PM|||| You don't have to balance your rear wheels unless you like to bounce and vibrate, also replace your wheels all the time (cupping, uneven tire wear, and the chance of dangerous handling).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><BR> Go to a "good" tire shop and see if they can get the wheels balanced only using inner weights. Good luck on this and keep us posted  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR>85GT (twoloud)||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||08-16-2001||03:45 PM||||Or you can have it balanced with stick on weights. they can go farther down toward the centerline of the rim instead of on the lip.||||reg||1
Z||000005||AL||08-17-2001||12:34 AM||||just get stick on weights for the inside, and a regular weight for the outside, just make sure they don't counter balance your tires.||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||08-17-2001||02:58 AM||||Do you like living?<P>!!!<P>Take your wheels to a good tyre shop (one that deals with aftermarket alloys, etc)<P>They will be able to blance your tyres with the 'stick on' weights, it will be good.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000007||fierovette||08-17-2001||07:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>Do you like living?<P>!!!<P>Take your wheels to a good tyre shop (one that deals with aftermarket alloys, etc)<P>They will be able to blance your tyres with the 'stick on' weights, it will be good.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierovette||08-17-2001||07:47 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>Do you like living?<P>!!!<P>Take your wheels to a good tyre shop (one that deals with aftermarket alloys, etc)<P>They will be able to blance your tyres with the 'stick on' weights, it will be good.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P></B>[/QUOTE<P>  OK, Thanks All I get the picture, Now, how about the fronts,, JUST KIDDIN. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||artherd||08-17-2001||08:05 AM||||Heh, well, do the fronts too :P)<P>Actually, the Fiero is especially sensative to even slightly imbalanced tires, make sure you stress this point to your shop, it's got to be exactly on or you'll be back :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>[/b][/QUOTE<P>  OK, Thanks All I get the picture, Now, how about the fronts,, JUST KIDDIN. <P>[/B][/QUOTE]<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
